{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, PCA, single) scored 0.485 acc and config_016 (multimodal, PCA+ResNet50, concat, single) scored 0.527 acc, showing a ~4.2% gain from adding the image modality. However, we lack the image-only baseline, so we cannot determine whether the multimodal gain reflects genuine cross-modal synergy or simply that the image carries stronger independent signal than RNA. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, ResNet50) completes the {RNA, Image, Both} comparison triangle under identical profile and encoder conditions, isolating the image's standalone contribution. Why this is the best next step: Without this baseline, we cannot judge whether the multimodal result is truly additive/synergistic or whether a simpler image-only model would suffice. This single clean comparison (removing only the RNA branch from config_016) reduces the most critical uncertainty before investing further experiments in more complex multimodal variants (multiprofile, alternative encoders, weighted fusion). It is the highest-information experiment per unit budget at this stage."
}

